{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/80105-cthonians-the-unliving-never-dead","id":80105,"title":"Cthonians; The Unliving Never-Dead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-26T01:10:41-08:00","id":80105,"title":"Cthonians; The Unliving Never-Dead","content":"Alright peeps. Its time to get some ideas strewn about, of Cthonians. I'm generally excited about these strange never-live-but-dead-anyway things, and i'de love to hear you guys thoughts on them.<br /> The way i interprid them, a Cthonian is the ghost of something that was never truely alive to begin with. Like the ghost of a language or the thought-form-god of a quasi-religion whose practioners were killed off before they had the chance to formalize their beliefs into a real religion. The unholy specters of dreams unfulfilled and the ghosts aspirations scorned.<br /> <br /> Since they're kind of esoteric and hard to really wrap your head around, i'de love to hear other peoples opinions on them. This is the thread for that.<br /> <br /> Cheers! ~ Krobeles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T01:30:24-08:00","id":80113,"title":"","content":"You know how they say a Geist is made up of a really old or powerful ghost a d something else? I always viewed Cthonians as that &quot;somthing else.&quot; Death spirits, essentially; everything from little incarnate versions of death-related ideas to the 'ghosts' of concepts, cultures, and ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T01:49:41-08:00","id":80115,"title":"","content":"Thats not a half bad idea. So essentially, in your interpretation, a Geist is born when a ghost devours a Chthonian?<br /> I suppose that would mean that the Geist essentially adopts the primary aspect of the Chthonian it ate, but tweaked to fit its own nature? Making that its new anchor? So if you had a powerful Ghost of a stab-victim, devour a Chthonian of a very particular and out-dated form of murder, you'de have a Geist of stab-murder? Simplified, of course...<br /> <br /> So then what would happen if a Geist kept eating Chthonians? If a Sin-Eater ate a Chthonian?<br /> Food for though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T02:05:21-08:00","id":80121,"title":"","content":"I've had one show up in my games, and left the distinct implication it was a remnent of an older age, or possibly older world. Mostly, I made it as creepy and bizarre as possible.<br /> <br /> As an aside, Summoners for Mage has some Cthonians in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T05:02:34-08:00","id":80163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/80105-cthonians-the-unliving-never-dead?p=80121#post80121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a remnent of an older age, or possibly older world.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you made them Cthulhu-esque?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T05:22:36-08:00","id":80174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/80105-cthonians-the-unliving-never-dead?p=80115#post80115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats not a half bad idea. So essentially, in your interpretation, a Geist is born when a ghost devours a Chthonian?<br /> I suppose that would mean that the Geist essentially adopts the primary aspect of the Chthonian it ate, but tweaked to fit its own nature? Making that its new anchor? So if you had a powerful Ghost of a stab-victim, devour a Chthonian of a very particular and out-dated form of murder, you'de have a Geist of stab-murder? Simplified, of course...<br /> <br /> So then what would happen if a Geist kept eating Chthonians? If a Sin-Eater ate a Chthonian?<br /> Food for though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Devours, melds, whatever verb you like that has the two become one, but essentially, yes.<br /> <br /> Geists are passionate creatures and like to push around Sin-Eaters. You might have the ghost of Mad Johnny, a violent criminal who <i>really fucking hated</i> being in prison. He rotted in a cell for years before dying, and sees his eternal stay in the Underworld as trading one prison for another. His rage grows and grows, and through some happenstance finds a <i>weird something</i> in some forgotten crypt-cave-castle that embodies, say, the old Aztec love of sacrificing prisoners to prove your dominance. Some mumbo jumbo happens and now the Aztec spirit and Mad Johnny are both gone; in their place is Big Dog, a geist who thrives on being free at all costs, especially if it means (violently) knocking down any and all competition. It's the idea of &quot;death as submission;<br /> Mad Johnny hated being dead, the Aztec spirit knew being murdered meant you had been conquered.<br /> <br /> It's not long before Big Dog finds some two-bit gangbanger bleeding out in a back alley and whispers in his ear, <i>&quot;You and me are gonna go far, kid. Right to the fucking top.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> ...or something like all that, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T10:13:59-08:00","id":80330,"title":"","content":"I'm fond of the notion of chthonians as <a href=\"http://wonsab.tumblr.com/post/67932522921/spitballing-on-the-nature-of-ghosts-and-gods\" target=\"_blank\">ghost-tapeworms.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T10:42:48-08:00","id":80348,"title":"","content":"In my almost complete but sadly neglected Geist Chronicles PDF I define Cthonians as a catch all term used by Sin-Eaters for anything in the underworld that can't be identified as another category. Possibilities include: ancient Ghosts, Ghosts of pre-human races, something dead that never lived, a dead idea or concept that cannot be understood because it's dead, or something even weirder.<br /> <br /> I also include a sample: The Conqueror Worms, giant worms that tunnel through the underworld eating ghosts and can enter and exit the Underworld by digging up to the surface or down into the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Baron Samedi - do you have any link to where I can see it in your write up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:08:57-08:00","id":80363,"title":"","content":"Think Cthonians can have numerous origins, but all of them are beings adapted to far reaches of the Underworld/Underworld like realms. For instance one of the implications of the Djet Relic is it slowly mutates ghosts into Cthonians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T01:43:29-07:00","id":88028,"title":"","content":"I am thinking of introducing (Somewhere down the line) a Cthonian from the Grave Dream. Essentially, it would be going on the concept of &quot;Death of Dreams&quot; as a general concept. &quot;Dreams&quot; in this case, wouldn't just mean the flights of fancy you get when you rest, but more abstract concepts of dreams, like &quot;My dream to one day become an accomplished writer!&quot; or &quot;My dream to become a better man than my father ever was!&quot;. I am not useing the Aspirations from GMC, but if i was, i supose it would mechanically void some of a characters Aspirations.<br /> The thing would have no face, form or voice of its own, and only use your own memories, regrets and nightmares to pressent itself and communicate (The vanishingly little it would even do so).<br /> <br /> If a person was struck down by this Dream Eater, he wouldn't be 'dead' in the conventional sense, but rather deprived of every last 'dream' he ever had, effectively rendering him with no dreams, no aspirations and no drive to do anything at all. He would still be live, sure, but the very concept of why it mattered to get up and do anything, would have lost all meaning to him.<br /> I would be taking some inspiration from The Quincunx from Mage; Summoners, in the sense that i would have its manifestation let the very notion of memory, drive and aspiration become fluid and lucid.<br /> <br /> It could force the characters to come to terms with what their true drives and motivations are, as well as forceing them to come to terms with old corpses in their closets and revive old regrets.<br /> <br /> My question though, is wether or not this actually seems like a believable Cthonian. I enjoy the hell out of the idea, but i just dont really know if it seems like something a Cthonian would be, or just some other wierd apparition from god-knows-where. Then again, if it dosen't, it could raise the question of just how closely other worlds are connected. If this thing (Which in this hypothetical scenario, dosen't seem like a Cthonian) crawled out of the Grave Dream, then perhaps the mind can act as a gateway, not just between the living world and the Underoworld, but perhaps stranger vistas? Arcadia? The Astral Realms?<br /> Still, hypothetical plot points aside, my question stands. Does this seem like something that would potentially be a Cthonian in your book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T11:36:56-07:00","id":88322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/80105-cthonians-the-unliving-never-dead?p=88028#post88028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, hypothetical plot points aside, my question stands. Does this seem like something that would potentially be a Cthonian in your book?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like the Nightmare from the Cahalith chapter of Werewolf's Signs of the Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T12:57:11-07:00","id":88379,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/80105-cthonians-the-unliving-never-dead?p=88322#post88322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like the Nightmare from the Cahalith chapter of Werewolf's Signs of the Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It does? I haven't read that book. Is this a good or a bad thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T13:22:34-07:00","id":88389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/80105-cthonians-the-unliving-never-dead?p=88379#post88379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does? I haven't read that book. Is this a good or a bad thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some quotes, to give you an idea:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Knauss wants me to talk about it. She wants me to tell her what it is. </span></span><b>I try to tell her, it is nothing. It is the antithesis. It is the unmade and it exists to feed off the void of dead spirits and steal our dreams from us. Its wish is to sever us forever from the glorious light of our Mother. It is hate. </b><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">But Knauss won't understand. Why won't she understand? Maybe it's gotten to her already. Maybe this whole place is a way for it to eat as many dreams as it wants. Dreameater. I wish you'd just kill me, you monster.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">It comes for me in my normal dreams now. Not just visions, but in my normal dreams. I have no choice but to ride with it, and let it burn away my mind. Let it gnaw away at my soul. I belong to it now, just another screaming face trapped under its beautiful pelt. </span></span><b>Let it consume me fast and be done with it. I don't want to live anymore without my dreams.</b> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">And these are from asylum wall-scrawlings, so you know they're legit.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T02:27:32-07:00","id":88728,"title":"","content":"Well. Fuck me. The publishers beat me to it. I supose its still doable, though? Its all about presentation, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T22:42:47-07:00","id":121506,"title":"","content":"Performing minor thread necromancy to share something interesting I stumbled across:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Livia Kohn (1993:148) describes the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigu_(avoiding_grains)#The_Three_Corpses_or_Worms\" target=\"_blank\">Three Corpses</a> as &quot;demonic supernatural creatures who feed on decay and are eager for the body to die altogether so they can devour it. Not only do they thus shorten the lifespan but they also delight in the decaying matter produced by the grains as they are digested in the intestines. If one is to attain long life, the three worms have to be starved, and the only way to do so is to avoid all grain.&quot;<br /> [\u2026]<br /> &quot;It is also said that there are Three Corpses in our bodies, which, though not corporeal, actually are of a type with our inner, ethereal breaths, the powers, the ghosts, and the gods. They want us to die prematurely. (After death they become a man's ghost and move about at will to where sacrifices and libations are being offered.)&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:02:19-07:00","id":125966,"title":"","content":"Mummies can summon up cthonians with one of their utterances in the core book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T09:29:31-07:00","id":127527,"title":"","content":"Have you been watching the new Cosmos? In it, NDT uses a neat little device to talk about the history of life on earth: the Halls of Extinction. Monuments to broken branches on the tree of life where in one fell swoop, massive amounts of species simply cease to be. Including one called &quot;The Great Dying&quot;, which killed out 90%-95% of ALL LIFE on the planet.<br /> <br /> Do you really think you can have that much death, that much agony, not make SOMETHING in the Underworld? Some amalgam thing, with a horrible kind of sentience from the death screams of millions, BILLIONS of plants, animals and everything in between?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}